# SSH Brute-Force Detection - Splunk SPL Queries
#
# Scenario: 01-ssh-bruteforce
# Data source: Ubuntu /var/log/auth.log
# Index: main
# Sourcetype: linux_secure


# ============================================================
# 1. Search for Failed SSH Authentication
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
# Identify SSH authentication events where the password
# authentication attempt failed.

index=main sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password"


# ============================================================
# 2. Extract Source IP Address
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
# Extract the source IP address from failed SSH events
# for further investigation.

index=main sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password"
| rex "Failed password for \S+ from (?<src_ip>\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)"


# ============================================================
# 3. Count Failed Attempts by Source IP
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
# Determine how many failed SSH authentication attempts
# originated from each source IP.

index=main sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password"
| rex "Failed password for \S+ from (?<src_ip>\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)"
| stats count by src_ip


# ============================================================
# 4. Basic SSH Brute-Force Detection
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
# Detect a potential brute-force pattern when the same
# source IP generates 5 or more failed SSH authentication
# attempts within the previous 5 minutes.

index=main sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password" earliest=-5m
| rex "Failed password for \S+ from (?<src_ip>\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)"
| stats count by src_ip
| where count >= 5


# ============================================================
# 5. Investigate a Specific Source IP
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
# Review all failed SSH authentication events associated
# with a specific source IP.
#
# Replace <SOURCE_IP> with the IP address being investigated.

index=main sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password" "<SOURCE_IP>"
| rex "Failed password for (?<user>\S+) from (?<src_ip>\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)"
| table _time host user src_ip source


# ============================================================
# 6. Review Failed Attempts Over Time
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
# Visualize the number of failed SSH authentication events
# over time.

index=main sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password"
| timechart span=1m count


# ============================================================
# Detection Notes
# ============================================================
#
# Threshold used in this lab:
#   >= 5 failed SSH authentication attempts
#   from the same source IP
#   within 5 minutes.
#
# This is a basic educational detection rule.
# Production environments should add additional context
# and correlation to reduce false positives.
